                    },
                    "message": "The new change looks good to me!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/Global/ConfirmModal.vue",
                    "line": 103,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "How does this enqueue feature actually works? There will be always only one confirm modal on performing an action I believe\nDo you have an example handy?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/Global/ConfirmModal.vue",
                    "line": 103,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "It is a defensive pattern to handle edge cases.  When a Dialog is closed, `onHidden()` calls `next()` to show any queued Dialogs.\n\nCurrently, I think that we're OK.  But when you consider batch items (like delete all logs) you could trigger a number of dialogs on the async API calls or responses.\n\nAlso consider that we'll add SSE support here really soon, and that will increase the chance async triggered code could spawn multiple dialogs (though that of course would be a bad pattern - to have an events stream launch blocking UI widgets...)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/Global/ConfirmModal.vue",
                    "line": 103,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "Hmm makes sense\nSeems like an extra feature\nNo harm in adding it"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Logs/Dumps/Dumps.vue",
                    "line": 351,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vedangi Mittal",
                        "email": "vedangimittal3004@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vedangimittal"
                    },
                    "message": "Autofocus functionality not working (probably because the confirm modal may not be in focus?) and on pressing \u2018Enter\u2019 multiple times the modal also keeps opening multiple times after selecting \u2018Cancel\u2019."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Logs/Dumps/Dumps.vue",
                    "line": 351,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Done\n\nUpdated patch:\n- Auto-focus configurable button when modal opens (cancel by default)\n- Enter key activates currently focused button\n\nTested dump dialog using only the keyboard from the dump page."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Logs/Dumps/Dumps.vue",
                    "line": 351,
                    "reviewer": {
